f2c2cc75f3ebc61c157eb1235fb5f6095e172386d6c102bf7756b5d3b22489","order":1,"original_content_hash":"sha256:63f2c2cc75f3ebc61c157eb1235fb5f6095e172386d6c102bf7756b5d3b22489","parser":{"profile_hash":"sha256:e2e630f5fc01efcdf753cee33ab534a1a102d128c099e0914b17ce10d3b0e26b"},"physical_order":1,"raw_blob_id":"28013e66-05cb-5b2d-a942-3769c495ee1c","raw_file_hash":"sha256:13ce632f5417fe6adf3597a0b967436e9f3daaf8e29b2aeca96c3f6955b2cc8d","source_chapter_id":"body","source_locator":{"container_path":null,"field":"text","offset_kind":"HTML_SELECTOR","original_byte_offset":null,"path":"hydraulics-15.html","record":1,"selector":".mt-content-container"},"text":"While all check valves serve the same basic purpose of allowing flow in one direction and blocking it in the other, their\ninternal design\ncan vary. The three most common types of check valves used in hydraulic systems are:\nFigure \\(\\PageIndex{1}\\): Three types of check valves: ball, poppet, and swing.\nBall Check Valves\nPoppet Check Valves\nSwing Check Valves\nFigure \\(\\PageIndex{2}\\): Schematic symbols with corresponding explanations.\nDespite their differences in design, these valves share the same\nschematic symbol\n, indicating their function remains consistent across various applications.\nFigure \\(\\PageIndex{3}\\): Schematic representation of a poppet check valve.\nA\npoppet-style check valve\nprovides a clear example of how these valves operate. Inside the valve body, a\nspring-loaded poppet\nrests against a\nseat\n, preventing flow in the checked direction. The spring is typically very light, meaning that only a\nsmall amount of pressure\nis needed to push the poppet off the seat and allow flow in the open direction.\nFigure \\(\\PageIndex{4}\\): Schematic representation of a poppet check valve with blocked flow direction.\nHowever, when fluid attempts to move in the reverse direction, it pushes the\npoppet more firmly against the seat\n, completely blocking flow. This design ensures\nminimal leakage\n, with many check valves providing a near\nzero-leakage seal\nin the checked direction.\nCheck valves, despite their small size, are indispensable in hydraulic circuits, contributing to both\noperational efficiency and system protection\n. By preventing unwanted flow conditions, they help maintain stable and controlled hydraulic performance.","title":"14.2: Types of Check Valves and Their Operation","volume":"","work_id":"hydraulics-15","work_title":"hydraulics-15"}],"work_id":"hydraulics-15"}